            <ArticleTitle>Successful outcome of Scedosporium apiospermum disseminated infection treated with voriconazole in a patient receiving corticosteroid therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1499-501</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A disseminated Scedosporium apiospermum infection was diagnosed in a woman with severe asthma and treated with corticosteroids. This fungi is resistant to fluconazole and amphotericin B. The infection was refractory to itraconazole, but responded successfully to voriconazole. A review of the literature is provided.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
